/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock is intentionally committed, not ignored — this workspace has
# binaries (sizing-bench, sizing-integration, sizing-cli) and pinned
# toolchain-workaround dependency versions (see SETUP.md
# "Toolchain note"), both of which benefit from reproducible builds more
# than a pure-library-only workspace would.

# sizing-py build artifacts (cdylib/.so land in target/, but a manual
# `cp` for local Python testing — see CHANGELOG.md's Session 8 entry —
# could leave one of these at the repo root)
*.so
*.pyd

# Editor/OS cruft
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
